-2. Key 1 and rectangular canvases require overrides rather than appearing in ordinary examples.
-3. Some nuisance axes remain correlated by the four-slot teaching schedule.
-4. Medium and hard have modest distribution separation.
-5. The executable rival set is finite; an undeclared shortcut may still exist.
-6. The high-volume oracle is a mirror corroborated by sampled Racket parity, not Racket on all 1,500 pairs.
