+
+For generator SHA-256 `b966566b12ca836cb93220215f1487130b6cecea073928ef94df5c5dd12d7273`, all nine base shapes have extent 3 along the copy-chain axis. Reflections and the vertical transpose preserve that extent. Consequently, the intended step length `marker distance + template extent - 1` and the plausible fixed rule `marker distance + 2` agree throughout current generated shape support. This is a support/generalization limit, not an observed failure on ordinary generated queries.
